        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "A tool for Apple technicians that made diagnostics easier in the 1990s is still useful today. Repairing this temperamental Macintosh SE was not yielding results. I lent my exhibit to a colleague who services vintage Mac computers. The Apple TechStep quickly revealed a list of hidden faults: a damaged serial port circuit and a faulty ADB chip. Because of this, the Mac could not complete its startup procedure and did not initialize the cursor."
